  "explanation": {
    "id": "f039b5a6-0659-48bb-a824-c5f35f8ecda2",
    "body": "In this question I made a typo in the split laplace transform of the differential equation into $\\frac{G(s)}{s^2+3s+2}+\\frac{2s+2}{s^2+3s+1}$. It should be $\\frac{G(s)}{s^2+3s+2}+\\frac{2s+2}{s^2+3s+2}$.\n\nI also mentioned at 2:56:56 that convolutions are not commutative. That is incorrect. They are in fact commutative so the order of your F(s) and G(s) will not make a difference. I just ordered the 2 functions as $F(s)\\cdot G(s)$ to match it up with the answer choices.",
    "questionId": "67eafdf7-3f19-44c0-9e04-8217c83f4a20",
